OrionLayer open fix 129 — a real pointer move during an injected click no longer rewrites it
============================================================================================

Work order 437, follow-up (26 November 2026): the residual loss of CANCEL_FIELD's right click
with the engine window shown and the physical pointer moving (9 of 12 with open fix 125 and
without it; 20 of 30 on the second measurement). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer`
(v2.0.1), after open fix 125. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp, ext_api.h,
src/game/platform.cpp.

Cause, from an engine trace of 30 right clicks. (1) The right click's help box is decided by
Check_Help_List (fields.cpp:3117), which reads the pointer at the time of the check
(mouse::Pointer_X/Y), not the position of the click; a left click uses the position of its press
(Check_Mouse_Buffer), which is why INJECT_CLICK was never hurt. (2) A real SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION
reaches Forward_Game_Mouse_State without ever reading g_injected_mouse_pending (the flag guards
only Sync_Mouse_State_From_SDL, which runs on focus gain, F10 and the fullscreen toggle): its
Enqueue_Mouse_Input_Event coalesces over the queued injected release (same buttons, 0) or a
later pump delivers the motion before the check, so the pointer is the physical one. (3) The
flag was cleared by the first Pump_Game_Input_Queue, which in the trace ran with 0 events drained
and the flag set, 55 ms before the SDL thread had turned the pushed DOWN/UP into queue events.
A hidden window gets no motion events, hence 30 of 30 there.

The change. Hold_Real_Mouse_() (set by all four injections, FilmGuard's release too) sets the
flag AND a deadline 300 ms ahead; Real_Mouse_Held() is true while the flag is set or the deadline
lies ahead; Sync_Mouse_State_From_SDL and the SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION branch stand aside while it
holds. The pump still clears the flag; the deadline is what outlives it.

Proved on a scratch clone with trace logging (27 of 30 before, 60 of 60 after), then on the
branch's build (linux-debug, 119 of 119 tests of linux-debug-asan-tests) in the game folder:
see doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md entry 129.

From 0a800387059c032c5e4ea0465aba1f4d3557f929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:31:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] OrionLayer Open Fix 129: a real pointer move during an
 injected click no longer rewrites it (the flag of open fixes 3/124/125 was
 cleared by the first pump, before the SDL thread had queued the click, and
 the SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION path never read it; with the window shown, a right
 click's help check read the moved pointer, 20 of 30 landed)

OrionLayer, open fix 129.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ext/ext_api.cpp   | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/ext/ext_api.h     | 11 +++++++++++
 src/game/platform.cpp |  9 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 1db1463e..5dda6d9b 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,22 @@ int16_t g_activated_input = 0;
 static bool g_pending_checked = false;
 static int16_t g_pending_rect[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};
 std::atomic<bool> g_injected_mouse_pending{false};  // OrionLayer, open fix 124.
+// OrionLayer, open fix 129. SDL_GetTicks() until which the real mouse stays held off after an injected click.
+static std::atomic<uint32_t> g_injected_mouse_hold_until{0};
+static constexpr uint32_t k_injected_mouse_hold_ms = 300;
+
+void Hold_Real_Mouse_() {
+    g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
+    g_injected_mouse_hold_until = (uint32_t)SDL_GetTicks() + k_injected_mouse_hold_ms;
+}
+
+bool Real_Mouse_Held() {
+    if (g_injected_mouse_pending) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    // Signed difference: still right after SDL_GetTicks() wraps.
+    return (int32_t)(g_injected_mouse_hold_until.load() - (uint32_t)SDL_GetTicks()) > 0;
+}
 // OrionLayer, open fix 112. An injected click's release, held while a film plays (FilmGuard).
 static SDL_Event g_film_release{};
 static bool g_film_release_pending = false;
@@ -3806,7 +3822,7 @@ static void ProcessInput() {
                 // coalescing rewrites the injected RELEASE to the
                 // physical mouse position, and the pointer has walked
                 // away before the game reads it.
-                g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
+                Hold_Real_Mouse_();
 
                 // The comment above has always said "in 640x480
                 // space" and until now that was a promise the code
@@ -3884,7 +3900,7 @@ static void ProcessInput() {
                 // CANCEL_FIELD right-clicks a field's CENTRE, which is
                 // the whole answer for a button and the wrong one for a
                 // grid field: the game reads xpos/ypos from the point.
-                g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
+                Hold_Real_Mouse_();
                 float wx = 0.0f;
                 float wy = 0.0f;
                 Game_Point_To_Window_Point_((float)cmd.param1,
@@ -3958,7 +3974,7 @@ static void ProcessInput() {
                 // mouse as the other two injections (INJECT_CLICK,
                 // INJECT_RIGHT_CLICK): without it the physical mouse
                 // rewrote this right click's release (open fix 3).
-                g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
+                Hold_Real_Mouse_();
                 float cx = 0.0f;
                 float cy = 0.0f;
                 Game_Point_To_Window_Point_(
@@ -4034,7 +4050,7 @@ FilmGuard::FilmGuard(const char* name)
 FilmGuard::~FilmGuard() {
     if (g_film_release_pending) {
         g_film_release_pending = false;
-        g_injected_mouse_pending = true;
+        Hold_Real_Mouse_();
         SDL_PushEvent(&g_film_release);
     }
     g_film = previous;
diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.h b/src/ext/ext_api.h
index a6d5df51..8669d16d 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.h
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.h
@@ -497,6 +497,17 @@ extern int16_t g_activated_input;
 /// reads it (Sync_Mouse_State_From_SDL).
 extern std::atomic<bool> g_injected_mouse_pending;
 
+/// OrionLayer, open fix 129. Holds the real mouse off for a fixed time after
+/// an injected click, instead of until the first Pump_Game_Input_Queue():
+/// the game thread pumps (and cleared the flag) before the SDL thread had
+/// even turned the injected DOWN/UP into queue events, and the right click's
+/// help box reads the pointer AT THE TIME OF THE CHECK (fields.cpp
+/// Check_Help_List), so one real SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION between the injected
+/// release and that check moved the pointer off the field. Set by every
+/// injection (Hold_Real_Mouse_), read by Real_Mouse_Held() on the SDL thread.
+void Hold_Real_Mouse_();
+bool Real_Mouse_Held();
+
 /// OrionLayer, open fix 71. True when timer::Release_Time may return at once:
 /// a battle is live, the engine's window is hidden (open fix 43), a client is
 /// connected to draw it, and no input poll (Tick) came since the last wait —
diff --git a/src/game/platform.cpp b/src/game/platform.cpp
index 12c0dba0..47a021b4 100755
--- a/src/game/platform.cpp
+++ b/src/game/platform.cpp
@@ -1054,7 +1054,7 @@ namespace platform {
             // over the injected release (same button state), pulling
             // the pointer back to the physical mouse. Stand aside
             // until the queue has been pumped.
-            if (ext::g_injected_mouse_pending) {
+            if (ext::Real_Mouse_Held()) {
                 return;
             }
 #endif
@@ -1401,6 +1401,13 @@ namespace platform {
             }
 
             if (event.type == SDL_EVENT_MOUSE_MOTION) {
+#ifdef ORION2RE_EXT
+                // OrionLayer, open fix 129. A real pointer move while an injected click is being delivered would
+                // coalesce over its release (Enqueue_Mouse_Input_Event) or move the pointer before the click is read.
+                if (ext::Real_Mouse_Held()) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+#endif
                 int16_t mouse_x = 0;
                 int16_t mouse_y = 0;
                 Map_Window_Point_To_Game_Point(event.motion.x, event.motion.y, &mouse_x, &mouse_y);
